, 6480)].\"\n        },\n        {\n            \"summary\": \"更昔洛韦 exhibits dangerous drug-drug interactions\",\n            \"explanation\": \"更昔洛韦 interacts with other medications, notably 氮芥 (mechlorethamine), a chemotherapeutic alkylating agent. Co-administration may lead to additive or synergistic toxicities, especially bone marrow suppression and nephrotoxicity. The interaction arises because both agents share overlapping adverse effect profiles, and their combined use can significantly amplify systemic damage. Additionally, co-formulation with acidic or alkaline drugs may cause precipitation and micro-particle formation, risking embolism and infusion reactions [Data: Entities (5821, 6292); Relationships (39248)].\"\n        },\n        {\n            \"summary\": \"更昔洛韦 is primarily indicated for 巨细胞病毒感染 but carries substantial risk-benefit trade-offs\",\n            \"explanation\": \"Despite its broad and severe adverse reaction profile, 更昔洛韦 remains indicated for the treatment of 巨细胞病毒感染 (cytomegalovirus infection), particularly in immunocompromised patients such as transplant recipients. Clinical reports note its effectiveness in managing viral symptoms, yet emphasize that benefits must be carefully weighed against the high incidence of hematologic, neurologic, and multi-organ toxicities. This risk-benefit balance is central to its clinical use and regulatory considerations [Data: Entities (5821, 798); Relationships (21671)].\"\n        }\n    ],\n    \"rating\": 8.5,\n    \"rating_explanation\": \"The impact severity rating is high due to the extensive, severe, and multi-system adverse reactions associated with 更昔洛韦, its contraindications in vulnerable populations, and potential for life-threatening drug interactions.\"\n}", "refusal": null, "role": "assistant", "annotations": null, "audio": null, "function_call": null, "tool_calls": null, "provider_specific_fields": {"refusal": null}}, "provider_specific_fields": {}}], "created": 1782120878, "model": "